---
// Privacy policy. Required for a Chrome Web Store listing; linked from the
// listing, the README and the front page. Keep it in step with what the code
// actually sends (utils/api.js is the only file that talks to the network).
import DocsLayout from '../layouts/DocsLayout.astro';
import { siteConfig } from '../../site.config.ts';
---
<DocsLayout title="Privacy policy" description="What BlankStare sends, where, and what it keeps.">
  <section class="doc-body" id="top">
    <h1 class="section-title">Privacy policy</h1>
    <p><em>Last updated 19 November 2026 · applies to BlankStare 0.8.0 and later.</em></p>

    <p>BlankStare has no server and no account. The author collects nothing:
    no analytics, no tracking, no usage data.</p>

    <h2>What leaves your computer, and only when you ask</h2>
    <p>When you ask for an explanation, BlankStare sends the text you selected
    (or the readable text of the page when you ask for a full-page summary, or
    a screenshot you pasted), plus any context or follow-up question you typed,
    to <b>one</b> AI service: the one answering at that moment. Which one depends
    on the keys you added and which free models are working today.</p>
    <ul>
      <li><b>OVHcloud</b> (oai.endpoints.kepler.ai.cloud.ovh.net), used with no
      key at all. OVHcloud's policy applies:
      <a href="https://www.ovhcloud.com/en/personal-data-protection/">ovhcloud.com/en/personal-data-protection</a>.</li>
      <li><b>Google Gemini</b> (generativelanguage.googleapis.com), only if you
      added a Gemini key. On Google's free tier, Google says it may use what you
      send and the answers to improve its products, and that human reviewers may
      read them. Do not select private or personal information when using it.
      Google's terms: <a href="https://ai.google.dev/gemini-api/terms">ai.google.dev/gemini-api/terms</a>.</li>
      <li><b>Groq</b> (api.groq.com), only if you added a Groq key. With the
      Orpheus voice, the English answer is also sent to Groq to be read aloud.
      Groq's policy: <a href="https://groq.com/privacy-policy/">groq.com/privacy-policy</a>.</li>
      <li><b>The Nein</b> (stravelakis.com), once a day: BlankStare downloads the
      public list of free AI models. Nothing about you or your text is sent.</li>
      <li><b>The providers' model lists</b>, once a day: BlankStare asks each AI
      service you use which models it offers, using your key where one is needed.
      No text of yours is sent.</li>
      <li><b>YouTube</b> (googleapis.com), only if you added a YouTube key and
      press Search: a search phrase based on your selection.</li>
      <li><b>Web search</b> opens DuckDuckGo in a new tab, as if you had typed the
      search there yourself.</li>
    </ul>

    <h2>What is stored</h2>
    <ul>
      <li><b>Settings and keys</b>: in Chrome's extension storage
      (<code>chrome.storage.sync</code>). If you have Chrome sync turned on,
      Google syncs these between your own devices, like your bookmarks.</li>
      <li><b>Today's model list, which models are resting, and today's count of
      explanations</b>: on this computer only (<code>chrome.storage.local</code>).</li>
      <li><b>Your last 20 answers</b>: in session storage, deleted when the
      browser closes.</li>
      <li>Nothing else. Removing the extension removes all of it.</li>
    </ul>

    <h2>Permissions</h2>
    <ul>
      <li><b>Read pages you visit</b>: needed so the button beside selected text
      is already on the page. BlankStare reads only your selection, or the page
      when you ask for a summary.</li>
      <li><b>Side panel, context menu, storage</b>: to show the panel, the
      right-click entry, and keep your settings.</li>
      <li><b>The AI services and The Nein listed above</b>: so BlankStare can
      reach them. It reaches no other site.</li>
    </ul>

    <p>BlankStare does not sell or share data, and does not use it for anything
    but answering you. Questions: <a href={`${siteConfig.repoUrl}/issues`}>open an issue</a>.</p>
  </section>
</DocsLayout>
